      <FanWeekendCtas lang="en" findHref="/visit/" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>This is a last-hour clock, not a three-hour table, not lunch, not the 14:00 explainer</h2>
      <p>
        Other pages already cover sitting an O’Reilly’s table for three spare hours from ~11:00, Sunday lunch then screens,
        the overnight clock from Saturday, and Four Corner’s own 14:00 opening page.
        This page is only the person whose watch says <strong>~13:00 — sixty minutes left</strong>.
        The two usual morning doors are already serving. The two 14:00 doors are the walk, not the sit.
        Do not re-promote Saturday 18:00–19:00 as still on.
      </p>

      <h2>13:00–14:00 — sit the two doors already on usual hours</h2>
      <p>
        O’Reilly’s usual from <strong>11:30</strong> (Pasaje de Matheu 4) — already open for an hour and a half.
        Dubliners usual Sunday from <strong>12:00</strong> (Espoz y Mina 7) — already open for an hour.
        Sit those two. Do not camp Calle de la Victoria before 14:00.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Reilly’s, Pasaje de Matheu 4.</strong>
          Last pint or a short sit under the passage. At 14:00: Four Corner is about <strong>2 min / 120–180 m</strong>;
          O’Connell’s usual Sunday door at Espoz y Mina 7 is about <strong>1 min / 40–80 m</strong> out of the passage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dubliners, Espoz y Mina 7.</strong>
          Named screens on What’s On — ask which game is on; we do not invent a 13:00 listing.
          At 14:00: O’Connell’s is the other door at the same number; Four Corner Victoria 6 is about <strong>1–2 min / 80–150 m</strong>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>14:00 — walk the two remaining doors</h2>
      <p>
        Leave the sit for the hour:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Four Corner — Calle de la Victoria 6.</strong>
          Opens Sunday 8 November from 14:00 until late, with sports screens. Not open before 14:00.
          We do not list which game is on there — ask at the door.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Connell’s — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7</strong> (Maps: O’Connell St).
          Usual Sunday door is 14:00. Today’s listing also from 12:00 — we do not invent hours.
          Pin the usual 14:00 hour as the walk with Four Corner. Meeting point; we do not copy Dubliners’ board onto this door.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Premier League from 15:00 is about two hours from now (Palace–Liverpool, Sunderland–Chelsea, Brighton–Brentford, Ipswich–Bournemouth),
        United–Villa 17:30, NFL afternoon/evening, and Atlético–Barcelona 21:00 sit on the same streets after that — coordinate, do not substitute.
        Named listings: Dubliners <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a> only. Ask which screen — not every game on every screen.
      </p>

      <h2>Last hour, then the 14:00 walk — addresses</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar — Pasaje de Matheu 4, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Sit now (usual from 11:30). Leave for 14:00. We do not invent a menu.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dubliners — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Sit now (usual Sunday from 12:00). Named Premier, NFL and Atleti listings on What’s On.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Four Corner — Calle de la Victoria 6, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Walk at 14:00. Sports screens. Not open before. About 2 min from Matheu / 1–2 min from Espoz y Mina 7.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Connell’s — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid</strong> (Maps listing: O’Connell St).
          Usual Sunday door 14:00 (today also listed from 12:00). Other door at the same number as Dubliners.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
      </ol>

